  [core/16-window-race.patch]
  Aether: tabs.query no longer explodes on half-created windows (group 16)
  
  The windowId/currentWindow/lastFocusedWindow path of
  WindowManagerBase.query wrapped uninitialised windows and
  activeTab/getTabs exploded (gBrowserInit undefined,
  browser-init.js not yet run). Now isBrowserWindowInitialized
  is required, same as getAll() does via
  browserWindows(false). An uninitialised window has no
  queryable tabs (same reasoning as Bug 1458918).
  
  [core/17-devtools-watchrace.patch]
  Aether: the DevTools watcher no longer explodes when the actor is gone (group 17)
  
  NotFoundError: No such JSProcessActor BrowserToolboxDevToolsProcess
  when opening privileged pages with the Console open, and when
  opening Ctrl+Shift+J twice. The actor unregisters itself on teardown
  (maybeUnregisterJSActors) while watch/unwatch/remove and destroy
  async flows are still in flight. The registry exposes
  isProcessActorRegistered() and the 8 paths (destroy, watchTargets,
  unwatchTargets, watchResources, unwatchResources,
  addOrSetDataEntry, removeDataEntry) do not touch processes without
  an actor. Without an actor there is nothing to watch/unwatch; the
  parent process targets are still updated. Leftover race NotFoundErrors
  (on use) are ignored; any other error is rethrown. DevToolsProcess
  Parent/Child sendQuery calls do not log NotFoundError (they fail
  silently and the caller ignores it). ContentProcessWatcherRegistry
  skips stale actorless sharedData entries during the bulk init (the
  query path already returned {error} and the parent ignores it).
  #onTargetAvailable ignores late targets from dead watchers, same as
  #onTargetDestroyed already did. Round 3: the child tolerates dead
  watchers outside queries (getWatcherDataObject returns undefined,
  getOrCreateConnectionForWatcher returns null, skips in the 4
  target-watchers, guards in receiveMessage). The synchronous getActor
  is resolved before the push with a skip (the .catch() did not catch
  synchronous throws). The same isTeardownRaceError predicate
  everywhere: NotFoundError (actor gone) and AbortError "destroyed
  before query" (actor destroyed with queries in flight).
  C++ (ReceiveRawMessage): messages for unregistered actors are
  discarded silently. Careful: ErrorCodeIs(NS_ERROR_DOM_NOT_FOUND_ERR)
  is not usable; ThrowNotFoundError stores
  NS_ERROR_INTERNAL_ERRORRESULT_DOMEXCEPTION in mResult. The absence
  of the protocol is checked in JSActorService, exactly here (same
  thread, synchronous stretch with no JS in between).
  
