-  font_smoothing_type:
-    type: quantity
-    unit: int
-    description: >
-      The system font-smoothing type, normalized across platforms: 0 = disabled,
-      1 = grayscale (standard), 2 = subpixel. On Windows this is the
-      subpixel-vs-grayscale type (SPI_GETFONTSMOOTHINGTYPE), distinct from
-      text_anti_aliasing (which records the ClearType contrast level). On Linux
-      it is the GNOME org.gnome.desktop.interface font-antialiasing setting
-      (rgba/grayscale/none). Not set on macOS (grayscale-only, no subpixel type)
-      or where the value cannot be determined.
